# Ensure shell scripts always check out with LF line endings, regardless of
# the platform's core.autocrlf setting — CRLF in a .sh file breaks it inside
# any Linux container/shell with "$'\r': command not found".
# See learning/01-hien-trang-va-danh-sach-loi.md#B-07.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf

# deploy/.env.example is meant to be `source`d by bash (scripts/e2e-local.sh does exactly
# that) even though its extension isn't .sh — `* text=auto` alone still lets Windows'
# core.autocrlf=true re-introduce CRLF on checkout, and a CRLF here breaks `source` the same
# way it breaks a .sh file: every "KEY=value\r" line fails to export at all, silently leaving
# the variable unset. Found by actually running the app after DB_PASSWORD came back empty and
# Postgres's SCRAM auth rejected it with a cryptic "Prohibited character" error, not by reading
# the file.
*.env.example text eol=lf
